WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:04.880
Unless you've spent the last eighty years
living in a Batcave, you probably already

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.580
know a whole lot about Batman: his origins,
his fancy gadgets, and his penchant for young

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.580
sidekicks.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.331
What you might not know is that an insane
series of events drove Batman to being the

00:00:14.331 --> 00:00:16.449
dark, brooding vigilante that he is today.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:20.230
Here are some of the craziest moments in Batman's
history.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.050
Zur-En-Arrh

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:27.340
In the mid-1950s, Batman began to have interdimensional
and outer space adventures instead of just

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.350
fighting street-level thugs and weirdos.

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:35.090
So, in Batman #113, our hero makes a strange
trip to visit a tattered, multicolored Batman

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.430
from Planet Zur-En-Arrh who needs Earth's
Batman's help fighting an alien invasion.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:44.030
Though Batman really should have just arrested
Zur-En-Arrh for his crimes against fashion.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:47.920
"You just booked your next vacation Rotul.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.130
A luxurious stay on the Zeta Alpha Nine prison
planet."

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:55.610
If this wasn't strange enough, modern Batman
writer Grant Morrison included the formerly

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:59.710
forgotten, insane adventure from Batman's
zany comics history into being some kind of

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:02.780
trip into Bruce Wayne’s personal Imagination
Land.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:07.330
Apparently, Batman himself created "Zur-En-Arrh"
Batman as a "back up personality" in case

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:12.350
he ever went insane—because people can be
backed up like hard drives, apparently.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:13.350
Bat-Mite

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:18.570
The following year, in Detective Comics #267,
Batman is visited from the Fifth Dimension

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:23.619
by an all-powerful imp named Bat-Mite who
absolutely worships the Dark Knight.

00:01:23.619 --> 00:01:26.590
“I’m your number one fan.”

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.479
“My fan.”

00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:30.580
“The biggest.”

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:35.500
Bat-Mite sets up increasingly strange challenges
so he can see his hero in action, including

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.939
making an enormous statue of Batman himself
come to life.

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:42.680
Naturally, Batman is annoyed by having another
little punk hanging around the Batcave, but

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.500
the guy persists on and off for the rest of
Batman's career.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.460
“What is it?”

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:51.409
Bat-baby

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:56.369
Batman endures dozens of unusual transformations
during the Silver Age, including periods of

00:01:56.369 --> 00:02:00.790
getting super old, turning into an ape and
a tiger, and being a genie.

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:06.260
However, few changes are so strange as Batman
#147's transformation into a...baby.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:11.400
Rather than taking the afternoon off, Batman
insists on wearing some suspenders and continuing

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.209
to fight crime, because if you thought a man
dressed as a bat was terrifying, a violent

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:16.890
baby is truly the stuff of nightmares.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.230
Like, can you punch it in self-defense or
what?

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.420
"Beh beh beh"

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.519
Zebra Batman

00:02:23.519 --> 00:02:26.309
Quick disclaimer: As an englishman we say
zebra not zebra.

00:02:26.309 --> 00:02:28.239
I was asked to record this part saying zebra.

00:02:28.239 --> 00:02:30.450
So just know that every time I say zebra I'm
dying inside.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.930
Thank you for your time.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:32.920
Anyways, Zebraman!

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:33.920
Eughh.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.700
Most cite Batman’s period of wearing rainbow-colored
outfits as his strangest, but his time as

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:40.349
a zebra-patterned crimefighter was even stranger.

00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:44.239
After going up against Zebra-Man, a guy in
black and white who can emit rays of magnetic

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:47.459
force, Batman and Robin go to investigate
the criminal’s lab.

00:02:47.459 --> 00:02:51.030
Because Robin is a Darwin Award waiting to
happen, he trips and zaps Batman with the

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:55.719
same machine that gave Zebra-Man his powers,
also giving him a similar suit in the process.

00:02:55.719 --> 00:03:00.059
As usual, Batman literally punches the stripes
off of Zebra-Man, and everything returns to

00:03:00.059 --> 00:03:01.059
normal.

00:03:01.059 --> 00:03:03.059
Well, relatively normal.

00:03:03.059 --> 00:03:04.319
Death of Robin

00:03:04.319 --> 00:03:09.019
After the Silver Age ended, the once-carefree
Batman of the '60s became darker.

00:03:09.019 --> 00:03:13.480
Everything reached a boiling point by 1988's
A Death in the Family: The Joker kidnaps Robin's

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:17.999
estranged, neglectful mother, beats Robin
nearly to death with a crowbar, and sets off

00:03:17.999 --> 00:03:18.999
a bomb.

00:03:18.999 --> 00:03:22.731
Readers at home were given the chance to call
a DC Comics hotline and let them know if they

00:03:22.731 --> 00:03:27.109
thought Robin should survive or go off to
that Batcave in the sky, and a slight majority

00:03:27.109 --> 00:03:30.640
of overwhelmingly bitter nerds decided that
Robin should bite the big one.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:35.519
Robin dies, and Batman sets out on a darker,
grimmer path from which he'd never recover.

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:37.139
Thanks, geeks.

00:03:37.139 --> 00:03:38.919
Killing Joke

00:03:38.919 --> 00:03:43.049
Because the Joker is on a mission to destroy
everything that Batman loves, he goes on his

00:03:43.049 --> 00:03:46.059
most malicious and personal crime spree in
Bat-history.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:50.939
In The Killing Joke, the Clown Prince of Crime
shoots Barbara Gordon, also known as Batgirl,

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:55.030
and paralyzes her permanently, before kidnapping
her father, Commissioner Gordon.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:59.469
The commissioner is kept naked in a cage with
circus freaks, and forced look at images of

00:03:59.469 --> 00:04:03.079
his daughter, naked and in agony from a gunshot
wound.

00:04:03.079 --> 00:04:08.309
Batman's entire world continues to fall apart,
and his real insanity begins to show through.

00:04:08.309 --> 00:04:09.459
Venom

00:04:09.459 --> 00:04:13.569
After accidentally letting a little girl drown,
Batman starts to use a strength-enhancing

00:04:13.569 --> 00:04:17.889
drug called Venom, knowing that it's a bad
idea, but willing to do anything to prevent

00:04:17.889 --> 00:04:18.889
another death.

00:04:18.889 --> 00:04:22.419
After realizing that his addiction is sending
him into an irrational rage and doing more

00:04:22.419 --> 00:04:27.700
harm than good, Batman locks himself the basement
for a month and detoxes by sheer willpower,

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:32.669
because damn, he's Batman—but a recovering
Batman is still a sight to behold.

00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:33.789
Knightfall

00:04:33.789 --> 00:04:38.020
Two years later, a criminal named Bane gets
ahold of the same drug that Batman was previously

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:43.629
abusing and uses it to enhance himself enough
to snap Batman's spine…

00:04:43.629 --> 00:04:44.699
“Bane”

00:04:44.699 --> 00:04:49.460
…but only after releasing all of the criminals
in Arkham to wear down the Caped Crusader

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:51.620
into a state of total exhaustion.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:55.759
Batman remains paralyzed for a while, while
a violent protege of his takes over the Batman

00:04:55.759 --> 00:04:59.680
name and causes the wrong kind of chaos for
Gotham's criminals, totally messing up the

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:00.680
Batman brand.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.250
Even worse than this guy.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.150
Batman wets his pants

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:09.370
If there's a single moment in Batman's complete
history that has no right to exist—including

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.570
this…

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:17.270
...it's Kevin Smith's comic tale in which
Batman wets his unitard because he stands

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.110
too close to an explosion.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:23.120
Because Smith lives in a world where adults
regularly cannot control their bodily functions,

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:25.830
Smith drags the Dark Knight into unforgivable
territory.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:30.270
He only makes it worse by openly discussing
Batman’s bedroom habits, and making Catwoman

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:33.610
have a temper tantrum once she learns that
Bruce is getting married.

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:36.419
Bob should have stayed silent on this one.

00:05:36.419 --> 00:05:37.969
Zapped through time

00:05:37.969 --> 00:05:42.590
Batman's time-travel adventures from the Silver
Age make a comeback when supervillain Darkseid

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:44.780
shoots the hero with his Omega Beams.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:48.880
Normally, these beams erase their victim from
existence, but this time they send Batman

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:52.510
back to the Stone Age, where he lives as a
caveman for a while, before slipping through

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:57.889
other eras in which he's a witch-hunter, a
pirate, a cowboy, and a 1930s detective.

00:05:57.889 --> 00:06:01.699
When Bruce Wayne eventually stumbles back
into present day after his epic journey, the

00:06:01.699 --> 00:06:05.669
Justice League has to stop his heart to prevent
dangerous Omega Energy from destroying the

00:06:05.669 --> 00:06:06.669
world anyhow.

00:06:06.669 --> 00:06:10.069
He survives, because Batman is the most badass
superhero ever.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.259
Thanks for watching!

00:06:11.259 --> 00:06:14.509
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:06:14.509 --> 00:06:18.219
And leave us a comment to let us know which
moment in Batman’s history you think is

00:06:18.219 --> 00:06:18.970
the craziest...

